WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:00.867
Breaking news,

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.201
the US

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.902
tracking a suspected Chinese spy

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.671
balloon flying over the United States.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.106
This is a picture of the balloon

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.041
and that that balloon

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.409
is the size of three busses

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.411
and it was over Billings, Montana.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.912
Video from our affiliate

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.214
in Billings also shows it

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.216
flying high in the sky over the city.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.318
Right. I mean, it's they're very visible.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:18.618
U.S.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.953
officials said the balloon was observed

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.222
over Montana after flying over Canada.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.757
President Biden has been briefed

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.591
on the situation.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:25.358
A senior defense

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.260
official says he requested options

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.429
on how to deal with the massive balloon.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.231
The military has so far decided

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:33.233
against shooting it down.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.434
It comes as the secretary of state,

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.735
Antony Blinken, is about to leave

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:36.936
for a visit to China.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.171
Oren Liebermann is OUTFRONT.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:38.571
And Oren,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.873
what more are you learning tonight

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.007
about this balloon,

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:41.474
which I mean,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.809
just to state the obvious here,

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.411
they decided not to shoot it down,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.378
but it's there, right?

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.080
I mean, it's still flying over the U.S.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.214
as we speak.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.682
And it has been for several days.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.283
The Pentagon says

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.484
they've been tracking this

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.952
since it entered U.S.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:53.853
airspace, essentially

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.588
coming in from over Canada.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.656
And they have been monitoring it

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.558
since then, even launching F-22

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.560
fighter jets to keep an eye on this.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.729
The Pentagon says it has traveled over

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.963
a number of sensitive sites

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.098
and although they won't specify

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.466
what those sites were.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:07.867
We already know that Montana,

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:08.435
for instance,

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.203
is home to ballistic missile silos.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.704
So it is possible that that's

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.839
what this balloon was going

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.507
after with its surveillance,

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.709
its intelligence gathering capabilities

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:17.377
as the Pentagon

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.712
keeps an eye to see where this is going

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:20.980
and what's happening here

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:21.848
and how it evolves

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.716
over the next several days here.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.150
The Pentagon

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.652
obviously very concerned about this.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.520
They do say this has happened

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.489
several times in the past.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.824
They haven't said when,

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:31.291
but they did

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.125
say it happened

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.393
in previous administrations.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.627
Of course, the key question is,

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:35.762
what do you do with this?

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.530
President Joe Biden was briefed about it.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.365
He asked for military options.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.567
But senior military leaders,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.835
including chairman of the Joint Chiefs,

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.703
General Mark Milley, advised against

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.005
shooting it down, at least for now.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.374
There is some risk to people

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.110
to essentially facilities on the ground

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.211
if you shoot it down.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.345
Not all that much.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.347
Montana isn't the most populated state,

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.381
but there is some.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:55.982
Crucially, though,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.350
the Pentagon says this doesn't

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.352
they don't believe this gives China

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.154
any huge surveillance or intelligence

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.088
gathering capabilities

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.823
over the satellites they already have.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.725
Yes. So I guess we're into that question.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.093
Do they know what it's doing

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.696
and why they're doing this now?

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.431
They don't have a specific answer

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.465
to that yet in terms

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.167
of what it's trying to gather.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.335
Is it controllable?

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:16.503
What is it looking for?

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.137
But obviously,

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.005
this has raised tensions at a time

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.073
when they're pretty much already

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.074
sky high.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.042
China reacting angrily to news

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.711
essentially just earlier today

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:25.345
that the U.S.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.112
has gained access

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.580
to more bases in the Philippines

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.949
we saw a similar angry reaction

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.251
with the announcement from the U.S.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.852
that they're essentially revamping

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.754
a Marine Corps facility in Okinawa,

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:35.688
right near Taiwan.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.624
So the tensions are already high here.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.692
This only adding to those tensions.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.161
The Pentagon says they have raised this

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.263
with China, both through the embassy here

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.531
and in Beijing.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.398
So that gives you an idea

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.666
of how angry they are.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.467
And they pointed out that

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.369
if they do assess the risk is growing,

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:51.471
they do have options.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.005
All right, Oren,

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.940
thank you very much for your reporting.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.708
And now let's go to retired

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.177
Air Force Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:59.312
He was stationed in Southeast Asia,

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.146
where he watched

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.681
China during his military career.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.049
So, Colonel Leighton, let's

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:03.783
look at this balloon,

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.185
that orange reporting on.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.953
It's the size of three busses

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.389
this is enormous, as Orange points out.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.723
China has satellites.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.058
They're watching the United States

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:12.725
all the time.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:13.893
So what is this thing about?

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.961
What is China doing here?

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.664
So one of the big things here

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.365
that China could be doing with

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.301
this is they could be scooping up

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.502
signals intelligence.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.002
In other words,

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.270
they're looking at our cell phone

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.339
traffic, looking at a radio traffic

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.741
they're looking at the government's

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.677
command and control networks.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.845
And it's or and pointed out

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.514
we have a ballistic missile

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:35.882
base, a series of ballistic

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.350
missile silos in Montana

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.886
and in North Dakota and Wyoming.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.521
So these are the kinds of things

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.488
that they could be looking at.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.623
Also,

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:44.724
they're probably looking

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.359
at these strategic bomber bases

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.660
that we have in the Dakotas.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.996
So this is something that

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.065
gives them a chance to perhaps

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.900
augment their satellite coverage.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.601
And it's

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.768
definitely a system

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.837
that could be collecting a lot of data.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.138
So that's what you're saying

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.473
is that there is more data

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.207
and specific

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:01.941
data signals

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:02.942
intelligence, cell phones

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:03.376
that they wouldn't

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.344
be able to get other ways

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.311
that they could get from this.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.713
And just to make the point clear,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.880
you're talking about the strategic

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.782
strategic bomber bases I'm sorry,

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.285
nuclear facilities.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.554
This was seen over Billings, Montana.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.555
And as Warren says,

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.023
there's not a lot of people there.

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.358
And that's part of the reason why

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:19.859
they are so strategically important

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:20.526
to the United States,

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.195
to our nuclear arsenal

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.097
and to the strategic bomber base.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.698
I mean, this location is

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.401
is hugely significant.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:28.935
It is.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:29.602
And, you know,

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:29.969
it's part

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.638
of what we call our nuclear triad,

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:32.972
which is made up of bombers,

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.574
missiles and submarines.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.476
So two parts of that triad

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:37.577
are right directly

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.946
in the path of this Chinese balloon.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:42.415
So I guess I'm curious

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:42.915
whether you think

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:43.950
they should shoot it down.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.118
I mean, it's just floating there

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:45.918
I mean, it's you know,

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.186
this is a real question.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.222
They've decided not to do that for now.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:51.224
What do you think about that?

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.492
And I know you also think

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:53.793
that China may actually be doing this

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.596
not just for itself, but for Putin.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.330
Yes.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:57.864
In fact,

00:04:57.864 --> 00:05:00.033
there is a very robust intelligence

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.134
sharing the relationship

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.002
between China and Russia.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.671
So one of the things that

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.372
you have to look at when it comes to

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.542
this is what kind of a diplomatic fiasco

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.311
it would be if you did shoot it down.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:11.477
You know,

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:12.245
there's a potential

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:14.814
that it could raise tensions even more

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.249
There is a potential, of course, that

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.950
if you did shoot it down at sea,

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.752
you know, it's already pointed out

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.220
there would be the possibility

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.323
of the loss of life on the ground.

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:24.057
So these are things

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:24.991
that have to be weighed.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.025
And if they believe

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.360
that they can mitigate

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.428
the collective efforts

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:29.295
and if they can make them

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:30.430
relatively meaningless

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.198
or relatively harmless,

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.633
then they usually opt

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.668
to let things like this fly over and

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.204
and let them assign to a lot of their

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.006
to their handlers.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:40.306
All right.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.341
Thank you very much, Colonel Late.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.275
And I appreciate your time.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:43.943
You better.

